{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -s 'https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pubmed&id=18711368,20952379,23562994,32404165,38347586,38438125,38622473&retmode=xml' | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" ?>\n<!DOCTYPE PubmedArticleSet PUBLIC \"-//NLM//DTD PubMedArticle, 1st January 2025//EN\" \"https://dtd.nlm.nih.gov/ncbi/pubmed/out/pubmed_250101.dtd\">\n<PubmedArticleSet>\n<PubmedArticle><MedlineCitation Status=\"MEDLINE\" Owner=\"NLM\" IndexingMethod=\"Manual\"><PMID Version=\"1\">18711368</PMID><DateCompleted><Year>2009</Year><Month>02</Month><Day>09</Day></DateCompleted><DateRevised><Year>2015</Year><Month>01</Month><Day>14</Day></DateRevised><Article PubModel=\"Print\"><Journal><ISSN IssnType=\"Print\">1061-4036</ISSN><JournalIssue CitedMedium=\"Print\"><Volume>40</Volume><Issue>9</Issue><PubDate><Year>2008</Year><Month>Sep</Month></PubDate></JournalIssue><Title>Nature genetics</Title><ISOAbbreviation>Nat Genet</ISOAbbreviation></Journal><ArticleTitle>tRNA splicing endonuclease mutations cause pontocerebellar hypoplasia.</ArticleTitle><Pagination><StartPage>1113</StartPage><EndPage>1118</EndPage><MedlinePgn>1113-8</MedlinePgn></Pagination><ELocationID EIdType=\"doi\" ValidYN=\"Y\">10.1038/ng.204</ELocationID><Abstract><AbstractText>Pontocerebellar hypoplasias (PCH) represent a group of neurodegenerative autosomal recessive disorders with prenatal onset, atrophy or hypoplasia of the cerebellum, hypoplasia of the ventral pons, microcephaly, variable neocortical atrophy and severe mental and motor impairments. In two subtypes, PCH2 and PCH4, we identified mutations in three of the four different subunits of the tRNA-splicing endonuclease complex. Our findings point to RNA processing as a new basic cellular impairment in neurological disorders.</AbstractText></Abstract><AuthorList CompleteYN=\"Y\"><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Budde</LastName><ForeName>Birgit S</ForeName><Initials>BS</Initials><AffiliationInfo><Affiliation>Cologne Center for Genomics and Institute for Genetics, University of Cologne, Cologne, Germany.</Affiliation></AffiliationInfo></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Namavar</LastName><ForeName>Yasmin</ForeName><Initials>Y</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Barth</LastName><ForeName>Peter G</ForeName><Initials>PG</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Poll-The</LastName><ForeName>Bwee Tien</ForeName><Initials>BT</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>N&#xfc;rnberg</LastName><ForeName>Gudrun</ForeName><Initials>G</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Becker</LastName><ForeName>Christian</ForeName><Initials>C</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>van Ruissen</LastName><ForeName>Fred</ForeName><Initials>F</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Weterman</LastName><ForeName>Marian A J</ForeName><Initials>MA</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Fluiter</LastName><ForeName>Kees</ForeName><Initials>K</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>te Beek</LastName><ForeName>Erik T</ForeName><Initials>ET</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Aronica</LastName><ForeName>Eleonora</ForeName><Initials>E</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>van der Knaap</LastName><ForeName>Marjo S</ForeName><Initials>MS</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>H&#xf6;hne</LastName><ForeName>Wolfgang</ForeName><Initials>W</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Toliat</LastName><ForeName>Mohammad Reza</ForeName><Initials>MR</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Crow</LastName><ForeName>Yanick J</ForeName><Initials>YJ</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Steinling</LastName><ForeName>Maja</ForeName><Initials>M</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\"Y\"><LastName>Voit</LastName><ForeName>Thomas</ForeName><Initials>T</Initials></Author><Author ValidYN=\